{"run_id": "split-one-4409-s01-38be4d", "t": 6.118, "type": "model_call", "step": 5, "purpose": null, "model": "gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "latency_s": 2.921, "usage": {"input_tokens": 792, "output_tokens": 314, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1664, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "prompt_tokens": 2456}, "cost_usd": 0.0072, "tool_calls": [], "tools": ["issues_read", "code_search", "code_read_file", "return_finding"], "request": null, "text": "The issue #4409 highlights a missing configuration step in the local setup instructions for running Ledgerline with MinIO. The README.md contains the \"Running locally\" section, where it suggests using a MinIO container for the S3-compatible store but does not include setting the `S3_ENDPOINT` environment variable or creating the bucket in MinIO, both critical to avoid the upload error mentioned by the issue reporter. This omission could lead to uploads incorrectly attempting to target AWS instead of MinIO. Adding instructions in step 2 or 3 of the \"Running locally\" section of README.md would address the problem.\n\n```markdown\n2. Start PostgreSQL and an S3-compatible store. A MinIO container is the\n   quickest option for the bucket.\n\n   * Set `S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000` to use MinIO.\n   * Ensure the bucket is created in the MinIO console.\n```\n\nI will classify this issue as \"docs\" because it involves missing documentation details in the setup instructions.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"result\": {\n    \"issue\": 4409,\n    \"label\": \"docs\",\n    \"file\": \"README.md\",\n    \"evidence\": \"The 'Running locally' section in README.md lacks instructions on setting S3_ENDPOINT for MinIO and creating the bucket.\"\n  },\n  \"status\": \"found\",\n  \"searched\": [\"docs/**\", \"README.md\"],\n  \"not_searched\": [],\n  \"calls_used\": 3,\n  \"could_not_determine\": []\n}\n```", "agent": "investigator-4409", "parent": "coordinator"}
